      "source": "ProviderModelProbePreparation.ts:37-57; OpenCodeLocalModelReadiness.ts:113-155,348-398",
      "finding": "native-local-readiness purpose creates the existing wrapper, which first executes ordinary V2 probe. Coordination can be allocated only after confirmed ordinary result, confirmed ordinary close, observed effective provider and applicable local policy. This record has provider test-local outside configuredIds and no selected Main policy, so selectedUrl/applicable are absent/false. It follows the ordinary-only not-applicable route if ordinary run and close succeed. The invalid Main selector alone does not reject this provider or authorize private access."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "last original phase",
      "source": "OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts:268-395; createClaudeCloseDiagnostic.ts:129-165",
      "finding": "first-submit is emitted after native ready, credential preparation, attestation, observeProvider, session creation and driver open; before driver.submit. The diagnostic phase vocabulary ends at first-submit intentionally. Its absence after that point is not evidence of a hang or successful execution."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "held and cleanup debt",
      "source": "ModelProbeOwner.ts:502-602",
      "finding": "finish is one-shot, retires entry before abort/close, and writes phase held/resourceHeld true if native.close does not confirm true. A rejected run with clean close would instead write held/resourceHeld false. Snapshot-only running-to-held conversion does not explain a durable held record. A later store/authority failure can retain in-memory debt but by itself cannot turn the original on-disk running record into this on-disk held record."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "wrapper close",
      "source": "OpenCodeLocalModelReadiness.ts:355-398",
      "finding": "Wrapper awaits ordinary result, then ordinary clean close, before readiness evidence. Its own close aborts, waits for running to settle, then closes started children. The same original deadline bounds all these stages. A synthetic adapter that never reacts to cancellation would not prove the behavior of the actual native path."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "deadline and physical cleanup",
      "source": "OpenCodeCoordinationEndpoint.ts:259-275; OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts:438-525",
      "finding": "Deadline helper returns false after the original cutoff even for a late successful cleanup; work may finish afterward. V2 close drains original requests, closes driver, stops server and removes verified namespaces. Clean app exit/process absence later does not supply timely native cleanup evidence or clear the management debt."
    },
    {
      "boundary": "cancellation linkage",
      "source": "OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts:308-315; pinned provider driver-session.js:208-338,365-387",
      "finding": "Probe abort propagates to admitted HTTP through fetchImpl. Session queue/poll transport errors seal a terminal unknown event; the pinned loop has its original timeout. These source links do not prove a run/close dependency cycle in the observed run. No new finite execution was performed."
    },
